---
name: kpi-audit-logs-canonical
description: Canonical audit table and workflow-status vocabulary for all KPI status-transition aggregations (RPCs, edge functions, migrations)
type: constraint
---
All per-KPI workflow timestamp / status-transition aggregations MUST read from `public.kpi_audit_logs` joined by the `kpi_id uuid` column. There is NO `public.audit_logs` table — using it is the BUG-031 defect that blanked the KPI Journey Timeline. Status literal filters on `(new_value->>'status')` MUST use the canonical vocabulary EXACTLY: `self_review`, `manager_check`, `skip_level_check`, `hr_pms_review`, `audit`, `management_review`, `kra_set`, `approved`. The deprecated literals `l1_review`, `auditor_review`, `skip_level_review` are forbidden. Why: trigger `log_kpi_status_transition` (migration 20251224061849_*) writes the canonical names into `kpi_audit_logs`, and `kpis.status` only ever holds those values. How to apply: when redefining any report RPC, grep the migration file for `FROM audit_logs` (must be 0 hits) and for the forbidden literals (must be 0 hits) before approval. Anchor: POLICY.md §104, DOCUMENTATION.md v2.66.7.33, src/test/bugBountyFixes.test.ts BUG-031.

UI rendering rule (added 2026-05-25, POLICY §126): one human action commonly produces 4–5 rows in the same TX because `safety_net_trigger` (`SUBMISSION_SCORE_CHANGED`), `log_kpi_status_transition` (`STATUS_TRANSITION`), and the `reconcile_workflow_statuses` tool (`RECONCILE_STATUS`) each insert their own row. Any timeline-style UI consumer of `kpi_audit_logs` MUST funnel rows through `groupTimelineEvents` (`src/lib/timelineGrouping.ts`) so cascade rows collapse under the originating human action behind a "Show system events (N)" expander. Do NOT drop side-effect rows at the DB or query layer — audit immutability is non-negotiable.
